Problem: Given that
\begin{align*}
\cos x + \cos y + \cos z &= 0, \\
\sin x + \sin y + \sin z &= 0,
\end{align*}find
\begin{align*}
&\tan^2 x + \tan^2 y + \tan^2 z - (\tan^2 x \tan^2 y + \tan^2 x \tan^2 z + \tan^2 y \tan^2 z) \\
&\quad  - 3 \tan^2 x \tan^2 y \tan^2 z.
\end{align*}

Solve step by step. End with: The answer is [your answer].
